    {
      "text": "There's no worse feeling than thinking you've finished doing the dishes and then spotting one more pot sitting on the countertop. I was wiping down the counter, feeling pretty good about myself. The sink was empty, everything looked clean, and I was ready to call it a night. I even had that small wave of satisfaction, the kind that makes you think, \"Yeah, I've got my life together.\" And then I saw it, that one pot just sitting there mocking me, still covered in whatever I'd cooked that night. For a second, I tried to ignore it. I thought, \"It's fine, I'll get it tomorrow,\" but I couldn't. It was right there, ruining my clean kitchen moment. So I let out that deep sigh. You know the one. Rolled up my sleeves again and started scrubbing. And that pot? Of course, it was the worst kind, the one that laughs at soap and needs actual effort to clean. My perfect moment was gone, but when I finally got it done, I stood there staring at the counter like I'd just finished a marathon. Tired, victorious, slightly annoyed, but also weirdly proud.",
      "start_time": 0.099,
      "end_time": 69.379,
